/*! \page dapp_quickstart OCUDU dApp Quickstart

This page is the end-to-end walkthrough for building an out-of-tree dApp
repository, packaging it, installing it into an OCUDU DU (gNB DU / O-DU)
catalog, enabling and disabling it, monitoring it, and verifying that it is
working. Working contracts remain ABI and package schema v1 until a formal
release decision.

Related pages:

- \ref dapp_operations — operator policy, signing, Class-B evaluation, process
  hardening, and the failure gallery
- \ref dapp_observability — metric and copy-accounting contract
- \ref dapp_release_provisioning — offline key custody, rollover, and revocation
- Git Markdown companion: \c docs/dapp/quickstart.md
- Standalone SDK document \c docs/ocudu_dapp_quickstart.md — scaffold detail
- SDK \c docs/class_a_cuda_authoring.md, \c class_b_accelerator_authoring.md,
  \c class_c_cuda_process_authoring.md, and \c observer_authority.md
- E3: \ref e3_management, \ref e3_wire, \ref e3_system_design

\section dapp_qs_model Mental model

OCUDU embeds one dApp Runtime inside the DU process. A dApp is not an external
side-car that the modem calls by path. It is a hash-bound catalog package that
the DU admits, preflights, and drives through a fixed lifecycle:

\code{.text}
out-of-tree dApp repo  --build-->  artifact + manifest-v1 + SPDX SBOM
                                         |
                                         v
                              operator catalog root
                                         |
                    (production) ocudu-dapp-package sign / trust
                                         |
                                         v
                    DU YAML: package_manifests (+ initial_instances)
                                         |
                                         v
         E3: load -> prepare -> arm -> shadow -> activate
                                         |
                                         v
              metrics / health / incidents  (prove it is working)
\endcode

Three timing classes share one management plane, not one real-time bus:

| Class | Role | Placement | Examples |
|-------|------|-----------|----------|
| A | Resident inline L1 | In-process only | CE, CE+EQ, full receiver |
| B | Bounded RT control | In-process authority | Scheduler intent / PRB avoid |
| C | Async observation | Native or supervised process | Spectrum, SRS--ISAC |

Hard safety rules:

- dApps never call each other; the host owns composition.
- E3 never supplies filesystem paths, executable arguments, or route descriptors.
- Conventional PHY and scheduler remain the fallback when a dApp is absent or fails.
- Production defaults require detached package signatures and an offline trust policy.
- \c ocudu_dapp_query_v1 stays pure; CUDA init, weights, and threads belong to lifecycle or model hooks.

Repository split:

- \b ocudu owns the public ABI headers (via install), runtime, E3, PHY and
  scheduler adapters, preflight, catalog, \c ocudu-dappctl, and
  \c ocudu-dapp-package.
- \b ocudu-dapp-sdk owns out-of-tree references, process helpers, scaffolds,
  certifiers, and authoring guides.
- \b Your dApp repository owns only the algorithm and package identity, and
  compiles exclusively against the installed \c OCUDUDAppSDK CMake package.

\section dapp_qs_build_ocudu Build OCUDU with dApp plugins

Configure a Release (or deployment) build with the dApp service and E3
management plane. CUDA is required only for resident Class-A CUDA packages and
CUDA Class-C paths:

\code{.sh}
cmake -S /path/to/ocudu -B /path/to/ocudu/build-dapp \
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$HOME/ocudu-install \
  -DENABLE_DAPP=ON \
  -DENABLE_E3=ON \
  -DENABLE_CUDA=ON
cmake --build /path/to/ocudu/build-dapp -j
cmake --install /path/to/ocudu/build-dapp
\endcode

Confirm the installed SDK package exists under the prefix
(\c lib/cmake/OCUDUDAppSDK). Without \c ENABLE_DAPP the DU has no dApp service
symbols. With the feature compiled in, omitting the YAML \c dapp: block still
leaves the modem path unchanged.

Build the standalone SDK once against that prefix so reference packages and
\c certify_class_a_cuda are available:

\code{.sh}
cmake -S /path/to/ocudu-dapp-sdk -B /path/to/ocudu-dapp-sdk/build-cuda \
  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=$HOME/ocudu-install \
  -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=121
cmake --build /path/to/ocudu-dapp-sdk/build-cuda -j
ctest --test-dir /path/to/ocudu-dapp-sdk/build-cuda --output-on-failure
\endcode

\section dapp_qs_new_repo Create a new dApp repository

\subsection Class-A CUDA scaffold (recommended product path)

Generate a new git root outside the SDK tree. The generator refuses to overwrite
an existing directory:

\code{.sh}
PACKAGE_ID="$(uuidgen)"
python3 /path/to/ocudu-dapp-sdk/tools/scaffold_class_a_cuda.py \
  --kind receiver \
  --target my_neural_rx_cuda \
  --global-name com.example.ran.neural-rx.cuda \
  --package-id "$PACKAGE_ID" \
  --vendor "Example Vendor" \
  --version 1 \
  --output $HOME/src/my-neural-rx-dapp
\endcode

| \c --kind | Interface | Output contract |
|-----------|-----------|-----------------|
| \c ce | \c 0x00010003 | Port-major channel + noise |
| \c equalizer | \c 0x00010004 | Compact symbols + post-EQ noise |
| \c receiver | \c 0x00010005 | Compact FP16 LLRs, pre-descramble |

The generated project:

- depends only on installed \c OCUDUDAppSDK;
- exports pure \c ocudu_dapp_query_v1;
- emits a shared object, hash-bound manifest-v1, and digest-bound SPDX 2.3 SBOM;
- keeps lifecycle and model shells in \c module_support.cpp so authors replace
  \c algorithm.cu.

Initialize version control in the new directory and keep signing private keys
out of the repository, CI artifacts, and DU images.

\subsection Class B and Class C

There is no separate scaffold binary for Class B or Class C. Copy one SDK
reference surface and rewrite package UUID, global name, vendor, version, and
CMake target names:

| Goal | SDK starting point |
|------|--------------------|
| Scheduler policy | \c reference/scheduler |
| Spectrum native | \c reference/spectrum or \c spectrum_cuda |
| Spectrum process | \c reference/process patterns for \c ref_spectrumd_* |
| Observer-only spectrum | \c ref_spectrum_observerd_cpu |
| SRS--ISAC | \c reference/srs_isac* and process variants |

See the corresponding SDK authoring pages for placement, backend, and
capability rules.

\section dapp_qs_implement Implement the package

\subsection Class A (resident)

Keep \c module.cpp as the pure query trampoline and \c module_support.cpp as
the lifecycle and dispatch shell. Replace only the algorithm entry and kernels
in \c algorithm.cu. On invoke: validate tensors, reject out-of-profile shapes,
enqueue only on \c invocation.execution_stream, write only caller-owned
outputs, and return without host-side stream synchronize, allocation, E3, or
blocking I/O. Allocate weights and scratch in prepare or model warm. The
reference v1 envelope admits up to two layers, all QAM, DM-RS types 1 and 2,
DC-capable operation, and no transform precoding.

Equalizer packages must write valid finite post-EQ noise: after equalizer-dApp
inline success the host derives scheduler-facing SINR from mean post-EQ noise
into CRC \c ul_sinr (resident CE stub leaves CSI empty; conventional E2E SINR
D2H is skipped). Host may set \c dmrs.reserved[0] to an optional OFDM-symbol
DMRS bitmask; packages may ignore it. Soft completion wall budgets default
to 2000 us (demod) / 800 us (CE); tests may inject tighter limits. See
Markdown \c docs/dapp/quickstart.md and SDK \c class_a_cuda_authoring.md.

\subsection Class B

The hook is synchronous, in-process, and host-record based. A package may use
CUDA internally but must still return complete host-visible intent inside the
deadline. Prefer \c scheduler_evaluation_only in the DU configuration while
measuring; that mode is ACTIVE and bound, yet conventional authority is
retained. It is not lifecycle SHADOW.

\subsection Class C

Producers never wait on consumers. Native placement shares the DU address
space; process placement uses credentialed shared-memory rings or a fixed CUDA
export pool. Exactly one spectrum result authority may be active; observers may
coexist. Process workers set Linux \c no_new_privs, answer authenticated
heartbeats, and release every lease before completion.

\section dapp_qs_certify Build, test, and certify offline

\code{.sh}
cd $HOME/src/my-neural-rx-dapp
cmake -S . -B build \
  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=$HOME/ocudu-install \
  -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=121
cmake --build build -j
\endcode

Expected products:

\code{.text}
build/my_neural_rx_cuda.so
build/my_neural_rx_cuda.manifest.json
build/my_neural_rx_cuda.spdx.json
\endcode

Run the offline Class-A positive certificate against the final DSO before the
package enters a DU catalog:

\code{.sh}
/path/to/ocudu-dapp-sdk/build-cuda/certify_class_a_cuda \
  build/my_neural_rx_cuda.so 0x00010005
\endcode

Preserve the JSON result beside the manifest. Extend the matrix with
deployment-specific shapes and model artifacts as needed. Compute Sanitizer
memcheck should use the default boundary shape set; racecheck may use
\c --shape-set compact.

\section dapp_qs_catalog Install into the DU catalog

Copy the three bound products together beneath an operator-controlled catalog
root. Do not rename the manifest without regenerating the hash binding.

\code{.sh}
export CATALOG=/opt/ocudu/dapps
mkdir -p "$CATALOG"
cp build/my_neural_rx_cuda.so \
   build/my_neural_rx_cuda.manifest.json \
   build/my_neural_rx_cuda.spdx.json \
   "$CATALOG/"
\endcode

\subsection Development unsigned admission

\c package_signature_mode: allow_unsigned admits a genuinely absent sidecar.
A present malformed, unknown-key, revoked, stale, or invalid signature still
fails closed. Do not provision production systems with this mode.

\subsection Production signed admission

Private keys remain offline with mode 0600:

\code{.sh}
ocudu-dapp-package keygen \
  --private-key /secure/operator-dapp-key.pem \
  --public-key /secure/operator-dapp-key.pub.pem
ocudu-dapp-package sign \
  --catalog-root /opt/ocudu/dapps \
  --manifest my_neural_rx_cuda.manifest.json \
  --private-key /secure/operator-dapp-key.pem \
  --package-sequence 1
ocudu-dapp-package trust \
  --output /etc/ocudu/dapp-trust.json --policy-epoch 1 \
  --public-key /secure/operator-dapp-key.pub.pem \
  --package <package-uuid>:1
ocudu-dapp-package inspect \
  --catalog-root /opt/ocudu/dapps \
  --manifest my_neural_rx_cuda.manifest.json \
  --trust-store /etc/ocudu/dapp-trust.json \
  --minimum-policy-epoch 1
\endcode

See \ref dapp_release_provisioning for custody, immutable generation, two-key
rollover, and installed-platform qualification.

\section dapp_qs_du_yaml Configure the gNB DU

The same \c dapp: schema is shared by dynamic, split-8, and split-7.2 DU
front-ends. List only catalog-relative manifests.

\subsection Minimum development configuration

\code{.yaml}
dapp:
  catalog_root: /opt/ocudu/dapps
  native_preflight_helper: /opt/ocudu/bin/ocudu-dapp-preflight  # absolute path, required
  package_signature_mode: allow_unsigned
  minimum_trust_policy_epoch: 0     # must be 0 when no trust store is configured
  package_manifests:
    - my_neural_rx_cuda.manifest.json
  local_e3:
    socket_path: /run/ocudu/dapp-management.sock
    request_timeout_ms: 1000
\endcode

\subsection Production-signed configuration

\code{.yaml}
dapp:
  catalog_root: /opt/ocudu/dapps
  native_preflight_helper: /opt/ocudu/bin/ocudu-dapp-preflight  # absolute path, required
  package_signature_mode: required
  package_trust_store: /etc/ocudu/dapp-trust.json
  minimum_trust_policy_epoch: 1
  package_manifests:
    - my_neural_rx_cuda.manifest.json
  local_e3:
    socket_path: /run/ocudu/dapp-management.sock
    request_timeout_ms: 1000
\endcode

\subsection Declarative instances at every DU start

Use \c initial_instances when packages must be present without racing radio
startup. Each entry names a manifest already listed under
\c package_manifests. Targets are only \c shadow and \c active. Startup is
synchronous, all-or-nothing, and completes before E3 ingress; any failure
unwinds every selected instance in reverse through deactivate, quiesce, and
unload.

\code{.yaml}
dapp:
  catalog_root: /opt/ocudu/dapps
  native_preflight_helper: /opt/ocudu/bin/ocudu-dapp-preflight  # absolute path, required
  package_signature_mode: allow_unsigned
  minimum_trust_policy_epoch: 0     # must be 0 when no trust store is configured
  package_manifests:
    - my_neural_rx_cuda.manifest.json
    - ref_spectrumd_cpu.manifest.json
  initial_instances:
    - package_manifest: my_neural_rx_cuda.manifest.json
      placement: in_process
      backend: cuda
      target: shadow
      lifecycle_timeout_ms: 1000
    - package_manifest: ref_spectrumd_cpu.manifest.json
      placement: out_of_process
      backend: cpu
      target: active
      lifecycle_timeout_ms: 2000
  local_e3:
    socket_path: /run/ocudu/dapp-management.sock
    request_timeout_ms: 1000
\endcode

\subsection Class-B evaluation-only mode

\code{.yaml}
dapp:
  scheduler_evaluation_only: true
  package_manifests:
    - ref_scheduler_cpu.manifest.json
  # ... catalog_root, local_e3, signatures as above ...
\endcode

\section dapp_qs_lifecycle Enable and disable at runtime

Management clients are \c ocudu-dappctl (C++) and
\c apps/tools/dappctl/ocudu_dappctl.py (Python/JSON). Both speak the same local
APER schema. Mutations are asynchronous jobs: wait for terminal success and
carry the returned instance generation into the next mutation. Stale
generations fail closed with conflict rather than applying twice.

\code{.sh}
export OCUDU_DAPP_E3_SOCKET=/run/ocudu/dapp-management.sock
DAPPCTL=(python3 /path/to/ocudu/apps/tools/dappctl/ocudu_dappctl.py
  --socket "$OCUDU_DAPP_E3_SOCKET"
  --schema /path/to/ocudu/schemas/e3/e3sm-ocudu-dapp-mgmt-v1.asn1
  --timeout-ms 2000)

"${DAPPCTL[@]}" inventory
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" load \
  --package <package-uuid> \
  --placement in-process \
  --backend cuda
\endcode

Lifecycle actions (C++ aliases in parentheses):

| Action | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| \c prepare | Create module state; still unbound |
| \c arm | Worker readiness |
| \c shadow (\c enter-shadow) | Warm without hook authority |
| \c activate (\c enable) | Bind hooks; path may use the dApp |
| \c deactivate (\c disable) | Remove authority; keep the instance |
| \c unload | Destroy after quiescence |
| \c retry (\c retry-quiescence) | Retry uncertain native quiescence |

Enable sequence:

\code{.sh}
# INSTANCE and GEN come from each completed job payload.
for action in prepare arm shadow activate; do
  "${DAPPCTL[@]}" lifecycle "$action" \
    --instance "$INSTANCE" \
    --expected-generation "$GEN" \
    --timeout-us 2000000
done
\endcode

For a new package, stop at \c shadow first, inspect inventory and metrics
schema, optionally stage a model, then \c activate.

Disable sequence:

\code{.sh}
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" lifecycle deactivate \
  --instance "$INSTANCE" --expected-generation "$GEN" --timeout-us 2000000
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" lifecycle unload \
  --instance "$INSTANCE" --expected-generation "$GEN" --timeout-us 2000000
\endcode

If native quiescence is uncertain, retry quiescence. Prefer a maintenance DU
restart over forcing resident code out of the address space while device work
may still be outstanding.

Disable without deleting catalog files: \c deactivate and optional \c unload,
or remove the package from \c initial_instances / \c package_manifests and
restart the DU. Full removal also deletes the three catalog products and
updates signed trust floors when signatures are required.

Receiver model path (while shadow or active, subject to package capabilities):

\code{.sh}
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" model stage \
  --instance "$INSTANCE" --expected-generation "$GEN" \
  --model neural-rx --version 1 --model-generation 1 \
  --artifact /secure/weights.bin
# then model validate, warm, activate with returned model generations
\endcode

\section dapp_qs_monitor Monitor

\code{.sh}
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" health
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" jobs list
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" metrics schema --instance "$INSTANCE"
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" metrics get --instance "$INSTANCE"
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" incidents list --instance "$INSTANCE" --limit 100
"${DAPPCTL[@]}" quiet-reservations --instance "$INSTANCE"
\endcode

Class-A host-owned signals include \c class_a.fallback.* (bypass before or
instead of trusting a result) and \c class_a.completion.deadline_misses (GPU
finished late; the current result was not conventionally replayed). Under UL
traffic with an equalizer package active, scheduler UE \c pusch_snr_db should
be present (not blank): the host derives it from mean post-EQ noise after
equalizer-dApp success. Class-B host measurements include
\c class_b.policy.invocations, \c class_b.policy.dapp_time_ns,
\c class_b.policy.deadline_misses, and related counters. Class-C process health
includes route publications, copy or export counters, heartbeat progress,
restart counts, and result protocol failures.
Observer workers must not emit map-shaped results; protocol failures are
security incidents. Metric name and unit contracts are defined in
\ref dapp_observability.

\section dapp_qs_verify Verify it is working

Work top-down and stop at the first hard failure.

\subsection Package admission

- \c inventory lists the package with expected interface, placement, backend,
  and capabilities.
- Production signature status is verified; package sequence and policy epoch
  match the trust store.
- \c ocudu-dapp-package inspect still accepts the staged artifact and SBOM digests.

\subsection Lifecycle

- \c load, \c prepare, \c arm, \c shadow, and \c activate succeed with advancing
  generations.
- Inventory reports state \c active.
- Management jobs reach terminal \c succeeded.

### Data path

| Class | Working means |
|-------|----------------|
| A | \c dapp.invoke.count advances under UL traffic; in-profile fallbacks are not spiking; completion deadline misses stay inside site policy |
| B | \c class_b.policy.invocations advances; no unexpected validation rejections; evaluation versus authority mode is intentional |
| C authority | Publications and accepted results advance; single-writer map present when declared |
| C observer | Publications consumed; zero map or result protocol emissions; heartbeats advance |

### Failure containment

- Conventional PHY or scheduler remains healthy when the dApp is deactivated or
  faults.
- Class-C worker kill restarts within bounds when process placement is used.
- \c deactivate / \c unload clear live authority without DU crash.

### Registered campaigns

\code{.sh}
ctest --test-dir /path/to/ocudu/build-dapp --output-on-failure \
  -R '^dapp_dummy_ru_e2e\.'
ctest --test-dir /path/to/ocudu/build-dapp --output-on-failure \
  -R '^dapp_dummy_ru_e2e\.operator_failure_gallery$'
\endcode

Class-A latency release admission uses
\c tests/benchmarks/dapp/run_class_a_cuda_qualification.py with an
operator-approved policy. A development report that fails only because controls
are unapproved is tooling evidence, not a field pass. Functional success in
this quickstart is not a production tail or multi-hour soak claim.

\section dapp_qs_recipe Lab recipe

Prove packaging first with the unmodified scaffold algorithm, then replace
\c algorithm.cu:

\code{.sh}
set -euo pipefail
OCUDU_PREFIX=$HOME/ocudu-install
SDK=/path/to/ocudu-dapp-sdk
DAPP=$HOME/src/my-neural-rx-dapp
CATALOG=/tmp/ocudu-dapps
PACKAGE_ID=$(uuidgen)

python3 $SDK/tools/scaffold_class_a_cuda.py \
  --kind receiver \
  --target my_neural_rx_cuda \
  --global-name com.example.ran.neural-rx.cuda \
  --package-id "$PACKAGE_ID" \
  --vendor "Example Vendor" \
  --version 1 \
  --output "$DAPP"

cmake -S "$DAPP" -B "$DAPP/build" \
  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$OCUDU_PREFIX" \
  -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=121
cmake --build "$DAPP/build" -j

$SDK/build-cuda/certify_class_a_cuda \
  "$DAPP/build/my_neural_rx_cuda.so" 0x00010005 \
  | tee "$DAPP/build/certify.json"

mkdir -p "$CATALOG"
cp "$DAPP/build/my_neural_rx_cuda".{so,manifest.json,spdx.json} "$CATALOG/"
# Point the DU YAML at $CATALOG, start the DU, then:
# inventory -> load -> prepare -> arm -> shadow -> activate -> metrics get
\endcode

\section dapp_qs_troubleshoot Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Likely cause | Response |
|---------|--------------|----------|
| Package missing from inventory | Wrong \c catalog_root or manifest name | Use catalog-relative names listed under \c package_manifests |
| Load fails signature | Trust sequence or epoch mismatch | \c ocudu-dapp-package inspect; raise sequence or update floors |
| Preflight timeout | CUDA init in query, or profiler on preflight | Keep query pure; do not treat relaxed preflight as qualification |
| Activate fails second spectrum authority | Single-writer map rule | Deactivate the current authority first |
| High \c class_a.fallback.* | Profile mismatch or open breaker | Inspect metrics schema and incidents |
| Only \c class_a.completion.deadline_misses | Late GPU completion | Optimize kernels or platform clocks; breaker may open on repeat |
| Process restart storm | Crash or heartbeat miss | Incidents \c processExit / \c heartbeatLoss; check limits |
| Generation conflict | Stale expected generation | Re-query inventory; retry with a new transaction |
| Unload quarantine | Uncertain native quiescence | \c lifecycle retry; maintenance restart if needed |

The deterministic operator failure gallery and its JSON report are described in
\ref dapp_operations.

\section dapp_qs_next Next steps

- Authoring depth: SDK Class-A/B/C and observer documents.
- Operator policy detail: \ref dapp_operations.
- Metrics contract: \ref dapp_observability.
- Release keys: \ref dapp_release_provisioning.
- Normative architecture: design-tree PDF
  \c ocudu_dapp_architecture_design.pdf.

All OCUDU-owned package, ABI, E3, FlatBuffers, and evidence contracts remain v1
until a formal release decision. SPDX 2.3 is the external SBOM format
identifier, not a local package version bump.
*/
